## Symptom

B292 cooldowns never apply to the hang class. exception Sync_watchdog is declared (c2c_relay_connector.ml:3097) and caught (3129) but NOTHING raises it - the per-root 3-strike wedge (3577-3597) only runs under injected mock sync_fns. A real hang trips the SIGALRM handler (3114-3127) which _exits with code 3 on the FIRST hang, killing the connector for all roots mid-sync: no wedge record is written, so after the supervisor restart the hung root is retried with no cooldown - a deterministic hang (slow relay, high-latency TLS) is an infinite crash loop at base cadence with zero learning, and each exit destroys all in-memory wedge/strike tables. Compounds with the at-most-once inbound handoff window (separate ticket).

## Fix direction

Persist a hang-wedge via an async-signal-safe write before exit, or run per-root sync in a forked child the parent can time out individually, or scale sync_watchdog_s with observed pass work (B291-style).

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17; verified by coordinator: grep shows no raiser of Sync_watchdog.